    "http://www.csun.edu/careers": {
      "title": "Join The Matadors",
      "description": "Careers @ CSUN | CSU Northridge Skip to main menu Skip to main content Labor Day Closure Read More Close CSUN California State University Northridge Search Form Search Submit Search Main Menu MyCSUN CSUN Portal Gmail Microsoft Office 365 Canvas Box Zoom Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Local Community Información en español Request Info Visit Apply Give Human Resources Careers CSUN California State University Northridge The Hiring Process Employment Application FAQs Troubleshooting Employee Notices Collective Bargaining Agreements Alternate Menu Search Form Search Submit Search MyCSUN CSUN Portal Gmail Microsoft Office 365 Canvas Box Zoom Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Local Community Información en español Request Info Visit Apply Give Human Resources Careers Home – Human Resources – Careers @ CSUN Join The Matadors In this Section Search CSUN Campus Job Opportunities by Keyword As a destination workplace, California State University, Northridge attracts, develops, and maintains a diverse workforce of over 4,000 engaged and committed faculty and staff. CSUN is committed to achieving excellence through teaching, scholarship, learning and inclusion. CSUN is especially interested in candidates who make contributions to equity and inclusion in the pursuit of excellence for all members of the university community. We invite you to explore your career opportunities to work with others who are making a difference. At CSUN, We Value: Commitment to Teaching, Scholarship, & Active Learning. Commitment to Excellence. Respect for All People. Alliances with the Community. Encouragement of Innovation, Experimentation, & Creativity. Learn more about CSUN’s Mission, Values, and Vision Find Your Career CSUN Staff & Management Opportunities Faculty, Coach, Counselor, & Librarian Opportunities View Lecturer Opportunities Academic & Non-Academic Student Opportunities Auxiliary Staff & Management Opportunities CSU System Wide Opportunities Benefits Based on your position, you could qualify to enjoy a comprehensive benefits package including health/medical, dental and vision benefits, retirement plans, tuition reduction, and other programs. Health, Dental, Vision Access to medical, dental, and vision insurance for you and your eligible dependents. Holidays Enjoy Work-Life Balance with up to 14 paid holidays and an additional Personal Holiday Well-Being Access to LifeMatters, your Employee Assistance Program for you and up to five members of your household Learning & Development Access to CSU Learn and LinkedIn Learning management platforms as well as online and In-person professional and personal development workshops. Fee Waiver Reduction Program Up to six (6) units of tuition coverage and fee reduction per semester for you or an eligible dependent. Total Compensation The Total Compensation Calculator demonstrates the significance of your CSU Benefits Package and how important it is to your salary. Resources FAQs To save time and submit your application as soon as possible, review the Frequently Asked Questions before contacting our office. Troubleshooting If you encounter problems in completing the on-line employment application process, here are a few tips to try. Collective Bargaining Agreements 95% of the CSU’s more than 63,000 faculty and staff are represented by one of 10 bargaining units. Employee Notices & Resources You can view Employee Notices that apply to current and prospective employees here as well as useful resources. The Hiring Process Employment applications are accepted only for current job vacancies and must be received online by the listed closing date and time. A separate employment application is required for each position. A resume may accompany the application, but will not substitute a completed application. CSUN Land Acknowledgement CSUN recognizes and acknowledges the Sesevitam, the first people of this ancestral and unceded territory of Sesevenga — which is now occupied by our institution. It honors their elders, past and present, and the Sesevitam descendants, who are citizens of the Fernandeño Tataviam Band of Mission Indians. We recognize that the Sesevitam are still here, and we are committed to lifting up their stories, culture and community. Equal Opportunity Employment Policy CSUN is an Equal Opportunity Employer and prohibits discrimination on the basis of Age, Disability (physical or mental), Gender, Gender Identity (including Nonbinary or Transgender), Gender Expression, Genetic Information, Marital Status, Medical Condition, Nationality, Pregnancy or related conditions, Race or Ethnicity (including color, caste, or ancestry), Religion or Religious Creed, Sex (including Sex Stereotyping or Sex Characteristics), Sexual Orientation, and Veteran or Military Status. Our nondiscrimination policy is set forth in the Interim CSU Nondiscrimination Policy . Reasonable accommodations will be provided for applicants with disabilities who self-disclose by contacting Recruitment Services at 818-677-2101. Office of Human Resources E-Mail Questions to applications@csun.edu Valera Hall 165 18111 Nordhoff Street Northridge, CA 91330-8229 Send email 18111 Nordhoff Street Northridge, CA 91330 Contact Us Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn A to Z Accessibility Directory Emergency Information Employment Maps & Parking The Soraya 88.5FM (KCSN) University Policies & Procedures Your Right to Know – Consumer Information Invest in the Leaders of Tomorrow Give Now © 2026 California State University Northridge Accessibility Title IX Terms & Conditions Non-discrimination Statement Privacy Policy Annual Security Report (CLERY) Annual Fire Safety Report Campus Safety Report Document Reader CSU System Scroll back to the top of the page"
    },
