e these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Division Job Number Closes Assistant Professor of Construction Management - Civil Engineering and Construction Management #27-08 Academic Affairs 561872 The Department of Civil Engineering and Construction Management invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Construction Management. Assistant Professor of Civil Engineering - Civil Engineering and Construction Management #27-09 Academic Affairs 561874 The Department of Civil Engineering and Construction Management invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Civil Engineering. Assistant Professor - Director of Forensics - Department of Communication Studies #27-10 Academic Affairs 561468 The Department of Communication Studies at California State University, Northridge invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor and Director of Forensics. The department seeks a teacher-scholar with experience coaching evidence-backed debate, mentoring diverse students, supporting inclusive pedagogy, and helping lead a forensics program committed to equity, public debate, and student success. Assistant Professor - Department of Management #27-04 Academic Affairs 560988 The Department of Management at California State University, Northridge (CSUN) is seeking a tenure-track faculty member in Management at the rank of Assistant Professor. The successful candidate will teach courses in organizational behavior, management, and/or human resources management. The successful candidate will conduct programmatic research in organizational behavior, industrial/organizational psychology, or a closely related field. Specific research interests are open, but preference will be given to those pursuing research that aligns with the research interests of current full-time faculty members of the Department of Management and that provides opportunities for collaboration among faculty. Assistant Professor of Information Systems - Department of Systems and Operations Management #27-06 Academic Affairs 561285 The Department of Systems and Operations Management at California State University, Northridge (CSUN) is seeking a tenure-track faculty member in Information Systems at the rank of Assistant Professor.\n\nThe successful candidate will teach related to Information Systems, Cybersecurity, Digital Forensics, Ethical Hacking, and AI Governance, and have research interests in Information Systems. \n\nIn addition to teaching, the position requires weekly office hours, attending faculty meetings, participation in assessment of student learning, and service to the department, college, and university. The successful candidate may be required to teach on weekdays, evenings, weekends, and/or online and will be held to the standards and requirements of the college and department in which he/she/they is/are housed for recommending tenure and promotion. Given CSUN’s commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and engagement in a diverse environment, the successful candidate will help the Department achieve equitable academic outcomes for all students through teaching, student mentorship, scholarship, and service. Assistant Professor - Taxation - Department of Accounting #27-11 (formerly #27-09) Academic Affairs 561198 The department of Accounting at California State University, Northridge (CSUN), is seeking a tenure-track faculty member in the Nazarian College of Business and Economics at the rank of Assistant Professor. The new hire will primarily teach Taxation and related fields.\n\nThe successful candidate will have research interests in Taxation and related fields. The position requires an ongoing program of scholarship in Taxation and maintaining the criterion for “Scholarly Academic” under AACSB’s accreditation requirement. \n\nIn addition to teaching, the position requires weekly office hours, attending faculty meetings, participation in assessment of student learning, and service to the department, college, and university. The successful candidate will be held to the standards and requirements of the college and department in which they are housed for recommending tenure and promotion. Given CSUN’s commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and engagement in a diverse environment, the successful candidate will help the Department achieve academic outcomes for all students through teaching, student mentorship, scholarship, and service. Assistant Professor - Audit - Department of Accounting #27-07 Academic Affairs 561017 The department of Accounting at the David Nazarian College of Business and Economics, California State University, Northridge (CSUN) is seeking two tenure-track faculty members in Audit at the rank of Assistant Professor.\n\nThe successful candidate will teach Audit, Data Analytics and/or Accounting courses and have research interests in Accounting and related fields. The position requires an ongoing program of scholarship in Accounting and maintaining the criterion for “Scholarly Academic” under AACSB’s accreditation requirement. \n\nIn addition to teaching and research, the position requires weekly office hours, attending faculty meetings, participation in assessment of student learning, and service to the department, college, and university. The successful candidate may be required to teach on weekdays, evenings, weekends, and/or online and will be held to the standards and requirements of the college and department in which he/she/they is/are housed for recommending tenure and promotion. Given CSUN’s commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and engagement in a diverse environment, the successful candidate will help the Department achieve equitable academic outcomes for all students through teaching, student mentorship, scholarship, and service. Assistant Professor of Acting - Department of Theatre Academic Affairs 560912 Tenure-track Assistant Professor of Acting with expertise in Acting for the Camera, responsible for training students in stage and on-camera performance while preparing them for professional careers across theatre, film, television, and streaming through instruction in acting technique, industry practices, and career development. Assistant Professor Finance, Financial Planning, and Insurance #27-03 Academic Affairs 560645 The department of Finance, Financial Planning, and Insurance at California State University, Northridge (CSUN) is seeking a tenure-track faculty member in Financial Planning at the rank of Assistant Professor.\n\nThe successful candidate will primarily teach Financial Planning and have research interests in Financial Planning and related fields. The new hire is expected to be actively involved in our CFP Board-registered financial planning program. Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry - Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry #27-02 Academic Affairs 560399 The department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at California State University, Northridge (CSUN) is seeking a tenure-track faculty member in Organic Chemistry at the rank of Assistant Professor. Assistant Professor - Department of Marketing #26-27 Academic Affairs 555736 The Department of Marketing at California State University, Northridge (CSUN) is seeking a tenure-track faculty member in Marketing at the rank of Assistant Professor.\nThe successful candidate will teach marketing courses—such as Consumer Behavior and Integrated Marketing Communications (IMC)—as well as other foundational courses as needed by the department, and have research interests and an active research pipeline in consumer behavior and related areas. Assistant Professor - Department of Business Law #27-01 Academic Affairs 558030 The department of Business Law at California State University, Northridge (CSUN) is seeking a tenure-track faculty member in 2027-2028 